The '''Spiritual mage''' is a potent [[Magic]] [[Slayer monsters|Slayer monster]] found in the [[God Wars Dungeon]]. Like all monsters there, they are aggressive to any players that do not wear items showing loyalty to their god. Spiritual mages require 83 [[Slayer]] to kill. Completion of [[Death Plateau]] is required before Spiritual creatures can be assigned as a [[Slayer task]].{{CiteTwitter|author=Mod Ash|url=https://twitter.com/JagexAsh/status/920581364457582592|date=18 October 2017|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/104356|archivedate=27 May 2020|quote=[can Spiritual Creatures be assigned as a task if Death Plateau hasn't been done?] No, they can't.}} Just like [[Spiritual ranger]]s and [[Spiritual warrior]]s, which require 63 and 68 Slayer respectively, there are spiritual mages for each god, and each one has unique stats.

Slaying a Spiritual mage in the God Wars Dungeon is a requirement for the [[Elite Fremennik Diary]] and slaying a Spiritual mage in the Wilderness God Wars Dungeon is a requirement for the [[Elite Wilderness Diary]].

Spiritual mages are best known for their [[dragon boots]] drop. They have fairly poor drops otherwise, with the original four god mages dropping a small supply of various runes. The Zarosian mages have a vastly improved drop table; more runes are dropped, particularly [[combination rune]]s, high-level herbs, a slightly increased drop rate of clue scrolls and most notably, the signature dragon boots are a tertiary drop from them.

The Zamorakian variant casts [[Flames of Zamorak]], which will drain a [[Magic]] level when it [[successful hit|successfully hits]] and deals damage to the player.

The Zarosian variant, being much stronger than the other four, casts spells from the [[Ancient Magicks]]; smoke inflicts [[poison]] starting at 4 damage, shadow lowers the player's [[Attack]] level by up to 15 levels (subsequent activations will not reapply until the player's Attack level is nearly restored), blood heals the mage for 20% of the damage dealt and ice freezes the player for 6 ticks (3.6 seconds).{{CiteDiscord|author=Mod Ash|url=https://discord.com/channels/324132423636090880/434286997360738305/1467836991453528145|date=02 February 2026|quote=Glacies and the Spritual Mages do 6 ticks, checking that your last freeze wore off over 5 ticks ago. Prayer doesn't appear to affect the duration. The accuracy roll is the NPC's magic accuracy vs the player's magic defence, which seems appropriate.
<br>Nex does 15 ticks, checking that your last freeze wore off over 5 ticks ago AND that you're not praying against magic. Prayer doesn't appear to affect the duration, once she's decided to apply it.|image=Ash_nex,_glacies,_spiritual_mages_freeze_duration.png|name=ash_freeze_duration|archiveurl=https://reldo.runescape.wiki/i/27962776#chat-messages-434286997360738305-1467836991453528145|archivedate=2026-03-07}} While damage from successful hits are blocked with [[Protect from Magic]], it does not stop secondary effects from occurring. This includes the blood spells, of which the healing is based on the damage dealt if prayers were not used.

